The data is loaded at runtime from a pinned commit and passed through by this
software with one modification to the requirement prose: OSCAL parameter
placeholders ("{{ insert: param, ... }}") are replaced with the text the BSI
defines for that parameter -- its OSCAL "values" entry where one exists,
otherwise the parameter's "label", which at the pinned commit is by far the
usual case. A label marks a value the BSI left to be fixed downstream, in an
adopting profile or by the using organisation, so the substituted span states a
placeholder rather than a settled value. The requirement it sits in is
unaffected. The German wording is otherwise verbatim -- nothing is translated,
summarised, or paraphrased.

